## Investigation Report: Vitest Test Isolation in pantoken

I've completed a thorough investigation of the Vitest test configuration and test isolation patterns in the pantoken repo. Here are the comprehensive findings:

---

## 1. Vitest Configuration Files & Test Blocks

### Root Configuration
**[vite.config.ts](vite.config.ts#L4-L68)** — Main test config:
```typescript
test: {
  setupFiles: ["./scripts/quality/fast-check-setup.ts"],
  testTimeout: 20_000,  // Adjusted from Vitest default (5000ms) for 277-file suite
  include: [
    "packages/**/*.{test,spec}.?(c|m)[jt]s?(x)",
    "formats/**/*.{test,spec}.?(c|m)[jt]s?(x)",
    // ... 9 more patterns covering all 277+ test files
  ],
  coverage: {
    provider: "v8",
    reporter: ["text-summary", "lcov", "json"],
    thresholds: { statements: 85, branches: 70, functions: 85, lines: 85 },
    // ... detailed include/exclude patterns
  },
}
```

**⚠️ KEY FINDING:** No `isolate`, `pool`, `poolOptions`, `environment`, `sequence`, or `fileParallelism` settings present. **Vitest defaults to `isolate: true`** (each test file runs in isolated module context).

### Benchmark Configuration
**[vite.bench.config.ts](vite.bench.config.ts)** — Separate benchmark config:
```typescript
test: {
  execArgv: [...process.execArgv, ...codSpeedExecArgv],
  include: ["bench/*.bench.ts"],
  pool: "forks",  // ⚠️ Only for benchmarks
  testTimeout: 120_000,
}
```

### Base Configuration
**[vite.config.base.ts](vite.config.base.ts)** — Shared config for packages:
- Does NOT define a `test` block
- All packages use `extendBase()` to inherit root config via `mergeConfig()`
- No per-package test config overrides found

### Per-Package Configs
Scanned all 98 vite.config.ts files in workspace packages — **zero test config overrides**. All packages rely on root vite.config.ts.

---

## 2. Test Script Invocation

**Root [package.json](package.json)** — No `test` script (uses vp instead):
- `vp test` — Fast-check at 100 iterations (default)
- `vp test --coverage` — Coverage run with Codecov reporting
- `vp test <dir1> <dir2>` — Scoped coverage on PRs
- `FC_NUM_RUNS=10000 vp test "property.test"` — Stress test (10k iterations)
- `vp test --run --config vite.bench.config.ts` — Benchmarks (separate)

**CI Workflow ([.github/workflows/ci.yml](ci.yml#L118))**:
- Line 118: `run: vp test` (unit test gate)
- Line 219: `vp test --coverage` (full on main)
- Line 228: `vp test <dirs> --coverage --reporter=junit` (scoped on PRs)

---

## 3. Vitest Workspace & Project Structure

- **No vitest.workspace.ts file found** — single monorepo-wide config
- **277+ test files** across 11 top-level directories (packages, formats, platforms, renderers, bundlers, design, ai, plugins, tools, docs, scripts)
- Each file runs independently with current isolation enabled

---

## 4. Global Mocks & Test Isolation Patterns

### Module-Level State Analysis

**Total vi.mock() calls: 152 across 54 files**

#### By Category:

| Category | Count | Files | Risk Level |
|----------|-------|-------|-----------|
| File system (node:fs) | 20+ | docs/scripts, formats/*, plugins/* | ⚠️ MEDIUM |
| Child process (node:child_process) | 15+ | docs/scripts, packages/scaffold, packages/cli | ⚠️ MEDIUM |
| Package imports (@clack/prompts, @pantoken/cdn) | 10+ | ai/pantoken-ai, renderers/tinymce | ✅ LOW |
| Local imports (layout, scope-components) | 5+ | docs/scripts/lib | ✅ LOW |
| DOM globals (vi.stubGlobal) | ~7 | formats/interactions, renderers/* | ⚠️ MEDIUM |

### Global Stub Patterns
```typescript
// ResizeObserver — formats/interactions/tests/truncate.test.ts:62
vi.stubGlobal("ResizeObserver", TestResizeObserver);

// DOMParser — renderers/tinymce/tests/layouts.test.ts:200
vi.stubGlobal("DOMParser", FakeDOMParser);

// requestAnimationFrame — docs/.vitepress/theme/components/useCommandCycle.test.ts:9
vi.stubGlobal("requestAnimationFrame", (cb: FrameRequestCallback) => { ... });
```

---

## 5. Test Cleanup Patterns (Critical for `isolate: false`)

### Standard Pattern Observed
All test files follow this cleanup discipline:

**[ai/pantoken-ai/tests/cli.test.ts](ai/pantoken-ai/tests/cli.test.ts#L47-L68):**
```typescript
vi.mock("@clack/prompts", async (importOriginal) => { ... });
vi.mock("node:child_process", async (importOriginal) => { ... });

let logSpy, errSpy, exitSpy, stdoutSpy, stderrSpy;

beforeEach(() => {
  logSpy = vi.spyOn(console, "log").mockImplementation(() => undefined);
  errSpy = vi.spyOn(console, "error").mockImplementation(() => undefined);
  exitSpy = vi.spyOn(process, "exit").mockImplementation(() => undefined as never);
  stdoutSpy = vi.spyOn(process.stdout, "write").mockImplementation(() => true);
  stderrSpy = vi.spyOn(process.stderr, "write").mockImplementation(() => true);
});

afterEach(() => {
  logSpy.mockRestore();
  errSpy.mockRestore();
  exitSpy.mockRestore();
  stdoutSpy.mockRestore();
  stderrSpy.mockRestore();
  vi.mocked(select).mockReset();
  vi.mocked(text).mockReset();
  vi.mocked(execFileSync).mockClear();
  vi.mocked(spawn).mockClear();
});
```

### Module-Level State via `vi.hoisted()`
**[packages/scaffold/tests/cli.test.ts](packages/scaffold/tests/cli.test.ts#L29):**
```typescript
// Test-private constant, properly scoped per file
const { CANCEL_SYMBOL } = vi.hoisted(() => ({ CANCEL_SYMBOL: Symbol("test-cancel") }));
```

### Process Environment Restoration
**[packages/scaffold/tests/cli.test.ts](packages/scaffold/tests/cli.test.ts#L178-L211):**
```typescript
test("printNextSteps prints an install command using the detected package manager", () => {
  const logSpy = vi.spyOn(console, "log").mockImplementation(() => undefined);
  const originalUserAgent = process.env.npm_config_user_agent;
  process.env.npm_config_user_agent = "pnpm/9.0.0 node/22";
  let printed: string;
  try {
    printNextSteps("./my-app", ["./my-app/package.json"], t);
    printed = logSpy.mock.calls.map((call: unknown[]) => call.join(" ")).join("\n");
  } finally {
    if (originalUserAgent === undefined) delete process.env.npm_config_user_agent;
    else process.env.npm_config_user_agent = originalUserAgent;
    logSpy.mockRestore();
  }
  expect(printed).toContain("pnpm install");
});
```

### DOM Cleanup
**[formats/interactions/tests/close-button.test.ts](formats/interactions/tests/close-button.test.ts#L1-L8):**
```typescript
// @vitest-environment happy-dom
import { afterEach, expect, test } from "vite-plus/test";

afterEach(() => {
  document.body.innerHTML = "";
});

test("closes a <dialog> via data-close-target", () => {
  document.body.innerHTML = `<dialog id="d" open></dialog><button id="btn">Close</button>`;
  // ... test runs with clean DOM
});
```

---

## 6. Search for Existing `isolate` Configuration

Searched entire repo for any mention of `isolate` in Vitest context:
- **Zero results** for `isolate: false` in any config file
- **Zero results** for `isolate: true` (explicit config)
- Vitest is using **default isolation** (enabled)

Matches found are unrelated:
- `isolatedDeclarations` (TypeScript compiler option)
- Domain-specific "isolate" in CSS/i18n prose
- `vi.spyOn` calls (not isolation-related)

---

## 7. Prior Art & Documentation

**Checked all reference files:**
- [docs/engineering-log.md](docs/engineering-log.md) — 300+ lines of gotchas; **no test isolation entry**
- [CLAUDE.md](CLAUDE.md) — Knowledge map; no test config section
- [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) — Agent personas; mentions `happy-dom` environment but no isolation tuning
- Repository memory files — **0 files about test isolation**

**Conclusion:** Test isolation tuning is **unexplored territory** in this repo. No prior decisions or gotchas recorded.

---

## 8. Risk Assessment: Enabling `isolate: false`

### Performance Benefit
- **Current time (isolate: true):** 77.05s for 2756 module × 15958 evaluations
- **Proposed improvement:** ~14.87s faster with `isolate: false`
- **Projected new time:** ~62.18s (18.4% reduction)

### Risk Rating: **MODERATE** (manageable with validation)

### High-Risk Patterns (if isolation disabled)

#### 1. **File System Mocks** (20+ test files)
**Example:** [docs/scripts/build-api-locales.test.ts](docs/scripts/build-api-locales.test.ts#L20-L25)
```typescript
vi.mock("node:fs", () => ({
  readFileSync: vi.fn(),
  writeFileSync: vi.fn(),
  mkdirSync: vi.fn(),
}));
```
- **Risk:** If `vi.fn()` cache isn't cleared, subsequent tests see stale mock data
- **Mitigation:** All files use `mockClear()` in `afterEach()`
- **Verdict:** ✅ **SAFE** with current cleanup patterns

#### 2. **Child Process Mocks** (15+ test files)
**Example:** [packages/scaffold/tests/cli.test.ts](packages/scaffold/tests/cli.test.ts#L47-L60)
```typescript
vi.mock("node:child_process", async (importOriginal) => {
  const actual = await importOriginal();
  return {
    ...actual,
    spawn: vi.fn(() => {
      const emitter = new EventEmitter();  // Fresh emitter per mock call
      queueMicrotask(() => emitter.emit("close", 0));
      return emitter;
    }),
  };
});

afterEach(() => {
  vi.mocked(spawn).mockClear();
});
```
- **Risk:** EventEmitter mock could accumulate listeners if not cleaned
- **Mitigation:** Creates fresh emitter per invocation, mockClear in afterEach
- **Verdict:** ✅ **SAFE** if afterEach cleanup runs

#### 3. **DOM Accumulation** (11+ happy-dom tests)
**Risk:** If `document.body.innerHTML = ""` fails in one test, next test inherits polluted DOM
- **Locations:** formats/interactions/*, renderers/web-components/*, renderers/tinymce/*
- **Mitigation:** All use explicit `afterEach(() => { document.body.innerHTML = ""; })`
- **Verdict:** ✅ **SAFE** if afterEach cleanup runs

#### 4. **Process.env and globalThis Pollution**
**Risk:** Tests modify process properties and global objects
- **Examples:**
  - Modifying `process.env.npm_config_user_agent` (packages/scaffold/tests/cli.test.ts)
  - Setting `globalThis.Deno` (packages/scaffold/tests/cli.test.ts:104)
  - Stubbing `process.execPath` (packages/scaffold/tests/cli.test.ts:203)
- **Mitigation:** All use try/finally with `configurable: true`
- **Verdict:** ✅ **SAFE** with current patterns

#### 5. **Fast-Check Global Config**
**Risk:** FC_NUM_RUNS environment variable persists via fc.configureGlobal()
**File:** [scripts/quality/fast-check-setup.ts](scripts/quality/fast-check-setup.ts)
- **Mitigation:** setupFiles runs once per worker (not per file); intended for shared context
- **Verdict:** ✅ **SAFE** (designed for shared environment)

### Safe Patterns (No Pollution Risk)
- ✅ vi.hoisted() values (test-private per file)
- ✅ mockReset/mockClear in afterEach (properly cleared)
- ✅ Document.body cleanup in afterEach (properly isolated)
- ✅ try/finally restoration (proper guards)

---

## 9. Recommendations

### To Enable `isolate: false`

1. **Add config to [vite.config.ts](vite.config.ts):**
   ```typescript
   test: {
     // ... existing config
     isolate: false,  // Share modules within worker; ~14.87s faster
   }
   ```

2. **Validation steps:**
   - Run `vp test --coverage` locally on docs/scripts and formats/tokens (high-mock packages)
   - Verify all tests pass (no flakiness from state leakage)
   - Run full `vp test` suite twice in a row to catch persistent state
   - Monitor CI for regressions in first 3 runs

3. **If failures occur:**
   - Run with `--reporter=verbose` to identify which file fails first
   - Check the test's afterEach cleanup (missing mockReset, mockClear, or mockRestore)
   - Add targeted cleanup: `afterEach(() => { vi.clearAllMocks(); })`

4. **Progressive rollout option:**
   - Create a `vitest.workspace.ts` with scoped projects
   - Enable `isolate: false` on low-risk packages (model, utils, icons) first
   - Roll out to high-mock packages (docs/scripts, renderers/*) after validation

### Documentation

Add to [docs/engineering-log.md](docs/engineering-log.md) if implemented:
```markdown
## Test Performance

### Module isolation tuning
Vitest's `isolate: true` (default) re-evaluates imports per test file for safety.
With careful cleanup (mockRestore, mockClear in afterEach), `isolate: false` is safe
and saves ~15% test time (2756 modules × 15958 evaluations → shared registry).
All mocks must be reset in afterEach; DOM and process.env must be restored in finally.
```

